WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.393
-Today is Friday,

00:00:01.393 --> 00:00:03.287
and that's usually when I catch
up with some personal stuff.

00:00:03.287 --> 00:00:05.338
You know, I check my inbox,
return some emails,

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.939
and of course I send out
thank-you notes.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:09.776
[ Cheers and applause ]
And I was running a bit behind.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.210
I just wondered
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.211
I'd just like to write out

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:13.345
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:13.345 --> 00:00:14.414
Is that okay with you?

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.282
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.219
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.253
[ Somber piano music plays ]

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.288
-No, no, no.
Something different.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.290
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:29.228
[ Happy piano music plays ]

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:30.463
[ Questlove laughs ]
-Ooh, wow.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:34.233
-Sounds like a level
of Mario Bros.,

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.202
where he's in, like, a
dreamland, like when Mario's --

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.637
-Get a coin, and he goes
into the drain.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.372
-Yeah. Let's go to the other.
I like the other one better.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.372
[ Somber music resumes ]

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:41.975
-Yeah, that's perfect.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.976
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:45.378
♪♪

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:47.813
♪♪

00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:49.649
Thank you, CDC,

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.185
loosening restrictions
for vaccinated Americans

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.486
for reintroducing the world

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.454
to the bizarre and elusive
concept

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.290
known as making plans.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.159
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:04.563
♪♪

00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:06.299
Thank you, Bernie Sanders

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.801
greeting Joe Biden
at his speech to Congress,

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.769
for being the first fist-bump
in history

00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:12.672
where you hear 10 knuckles
crack at once.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:16.242
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.510
"My hand!"

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.379
-"My hand fell off."

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:22.115
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.349
"Here, take mine."

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.385
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.287
♪♪

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:30.422
Thank you, the Kentucky Derby,

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:33.859
for letting me know what NASCAR
would look like in 1896.

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:37.530
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.966
-Hurdle by a stretch.
[ Hoofbeats ]

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.602
-And the winner is Beetlebaum.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.171
♪♪

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.306
Thank you, mint juleps,

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.475
for being the closest
I've come to eating a salad

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:50.877
in the last three months.

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:53.513
Yum.
-Minty.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.716
For you health.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.084
♪♪

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:01.553
-Thank you, number-one NFL Draft
pick Trevor Lawrence,

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:03.055
for being the first quarterback

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:06.626
to get an endorsement deal for
both Nike and Garnier Fructis.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.328
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.063
[ Applause ]
-My gosh.

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.499
-I won!

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.868
♪♪

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.569
Thank you, lox,

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:20.139
for tricking me
into eating sushi at 9:00 a.m.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.041
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.076
[ Applause ]
Nice try.

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:25.945
-Glad you thanked lox.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.414
♪♪

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.383
-Thank you, U.S. Census,

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:33.620
for being the government's
version of a nosy neighbor.

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:36.623
He lives with how many people?

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:39.758
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.758 --> 00:02:40.927
-All right.
-Okay.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.162
Just don't see
that many cars there.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.264
Interesting.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.599
♪♪

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:49.135
Thank you, The Census Bureau,

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.737
for sounding like an '80s
New Wave band

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:53.005
that never quite hit it big.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:54.407
[ British accent ]
"We're The Census Bureau."

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.642
♪♪

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.711
"This is our first song.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.112
We love you.
We're The Census Bureau.

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:01.747
Good night, everybody!"

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:02.849
♪♪

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.517
♪ I gotta get to the Derby ♪

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.985
♪ Gotta go real hard ♪

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.620
♪ I gotta get to the Derby ♪

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.054
♪ I don't have a car ♪

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:11.024
♪ At least The Census
don't know ♪

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.260
♪ I said
The Census don't know ♪

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.462
-♪ The Census don't know ♪

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.864
-[ Deep voice ] ♪ Listerine ♪

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.532
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.833
[ Somber music resumes ]

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.903
-[ Normal voice ] Thank you,
racing hoods for horses,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.906
or, as horses say,
"Guess who's Zorro now, bisch?"

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.641
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:29.641
What?

00:03:29.641 --> 00:03:30.810
-That's what they say?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.045
-I have no idea. I have no idea.

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:35.047
-And you're thanking them
for it?

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:37.049
-[ Chuckles ]

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.318
-You thanked a horse...

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.319
-What's that?
-[Laughing] ...for saying...

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:41.688
-Yep.
-...for saying,

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:45.024
"Look who's Zorro now, bisch?"
Okay.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.292
♪♪

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.395
-Thank you, toasters,
for having two settings --

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.864
raw dough and volcano rock.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.099
There you have it.
Those are my thank-you notes.

